A||||3||jch82||Oil pressure???||||5||
Z||000000||jch82||07-14-2001||08:15 PM||||Okay, the other day, Ken and I went for a ride in my fiero. It's an 85GT, 2.8 4speed. After the engine warms up, the oil pressure drops to about 1/4 and when I hit the gas, it will rise to about 3/4's. There is a little bit of bearing noise but only on takeoff and when the oil pressure is low...Could my oil pump be the problem and if so, would a high volume oil pump get rid of the bearing noise???<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||07-14-2001||10:52 PM||||sounds like a bearing is on its way out. I would suggest you change your oil immediately to a heavier grade of oil. I don't believe the pump is the problem the gauge readings you are describing sound normal.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||07-14-2001||10:58 PM||||"Bearing noise" most likely means rebuild time. heavier oil may help quiet it but won't prevent the inevitable. Same for high volume pump.||||reg||1
Z||000003||jch82||07-15-2001||12:45 AM||||Well I guess I will just use a heavier grade of oil but I really only need the engine to last the rest of this summer because I plan on buying a low mileage 2.8 come fall and finish up my car by next year. Thanks for the help!<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
